  "description": "Fast, zero-dependency conversion between DataTable/DataRow and your classes: map rows to models with case-insensitive columns and automatic type conversion, and turn any IEnumerable<T> into a DataTable. Supports .NET Framework 3.5 through .NET 10.",
  "id": "Fayakun.Extensions.DataTable",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-09T12:49:14.13Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "YwWr/re9L/xFLYiCq1GTIEUKxUs/3cu9GHjsNkfkl6Zz56RAYhEzXzq6o3MGRRgkYmWNXl/Kj6xxkBdqAqmbzA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 95051,
  "published": "2026-11-09T12:45:00.02Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.1.0\n- New: IEnumerable<T>.ToDataTable() creates a typed DataTable from any collection.\n- New targets: netcoreapp3.1, net6.0, net8.0 and net10.0.\n- Much faster: property maps are built once per type, columns are resolved once per table, and setters are compiled (.NET Framework 4.0+).\n- Column names are matched case-insensitively, and an exact-case match wins.\n- Values are converted to the property type: numeric widening and narrowing, Nullable<T>, enums (from names or numbers), Guid, DateTimeOffset, TimeSpan and bool.\n- AsEnumerable<T>() is now lazy and maps rows as they are enumerated.\n- Read-only and indexer properties are skipped instead of throwing.\n- Conversion failures throw InvalidCastException naming the column and property.",
